package-lock.json
# ...except the published npm package's, which is committed on purpose: `runNpmTests` installs with
# `npm ci` so a CI run resolves the tree this file pins rather than whatever the registry serves
# that day. Without it, a package we do not use can break the build - `vitest` declares `happy-dom`,
# `jsdom` and `@edge-runtime/vm` as wildcard optional peers, npm walks them anyway, and a publish
# into that closure on 2026-09-03 crashed the resolver for every branch at once.
# Regenerate it (`npm install` in that directory) whenever its package.json changes; `npm ci` fails
# loudly if the two disagree, which is the point.
!scalus-cardano-ledger/js/src/main/npm/package-lock.json
